PATCH 339: FUN_1000_ab7f -- the per-object DRAW-MODE state machine (an ab03 frame-phase animation twin,
0x98fc/0x98dc -> ab82 -> ab7f), object + class-descriptor near-offset base-loss.  The task-named twin.
The crash MIGRATED here (chain c0e5->7c1d->ab03->ab82->ab7f, fault ~0xcb78) once patches 335-338 cleared
the shallower c0e5->b5e7->addb->a18e->0731 chain.

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin @ 0x1ab7f-0x1ac09; DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00; seg-0xf69):
ab03 (patch 246) dispatches its frame-phase method keeping the OBJECT in DI (delivered as arg0); ab82
forwards it to ab7f as param_1.  ab7f reads [di+0x40/0x19/0x45/0x97/0x1c] and writes the draw-mode
selector obj[0x43], and consults the class descriptor DAT_2000_5796 (DGROUP:0x9796, a NEAR OFFSET written
by ab03).  Ghidra dereferenced param_1 as a host pointer (SIGSEGV at [di+0x40]) and DAT_2000_5796 (and
its *DAT_2000_5796 / DAT_2000_5796[1] chases) as host pointers.  Same class as aa08/a9b9 (patch 334).

THE FIX: object = g_mem+0x1c000+di; A = word[DGROUP:0x9796]; *DAT_2000_5796 = word[DGROUP:A],
DAT_2000_5796[1] = word[DGROUP:A+2]; the -0x66ba/-0x66aa rank-table byte reads rebased to DGROUP; b26a
returns the rank byte in AL.  Mission-cascade only (the 459a flight tick) -> behaviour-neutral for the
24 verify flows.
